# FreeBSD Emulation Framework - Example Configurations

This directory contains example configuration files for the FreeBSD emulation
framework at different security levels. Choose the configuration that best
matches your use case.

## Configuration Files

| File | Security Level | Use Case |
|------|---------------|----------|
| `emu-basic.conf` | Insecure | Local development, isolated testing |
| `emu-standard.conf` | Standard | Development servers, general use |
| `emu-high.conf` | High | Production servers, sensitive data |
| `emu-maximum.conf` | Maximum | Critical infrastructure, highest security |

## Security Level Comparison

| Feature | Basic | Standard | High | Maximum |
|---------|-------|----------|------|---------|
| Securelevel | -1 | 1 | 3 | 3 |
| MAC Enforcement | Off | On | On | On |
| Veriexec Check | Off | Auto | On | On |
| Audit Logging | Off | On | On | On |
| Network Isolation | Off | Off | On | On |
| Swap Encryption | Off | Off | On | On |
| Memory Encryption | Off | Off | On | On |
| Huge Pages | Off | Auto | On | On |
| NUMA Awareness | Off | On | On | On |
| RCTL Limits | Off | On | On | On |
| Max Instances | 128 | 32 | 16 | 8 |
| Max Memory (MB) | 131072 | 65536 | 32768 | 16384 |

## Installation

1. Choose the configuration matching your security requirements:

   ```bash
   # For development (insecure)
   cp emu-basic.conf /usr/local/etc/emu/emu.conf

   # For production (high security)
   cp emu-high.conf /usr/local/etc/emu/emu.conf
   ```

2. Review and adjust settings as needed for your environment.

3. Create required directories:

   ```bash
   mkdir -p /var/emu /var/cache/emu/images
   chmod 750 /var/emu /var/cache/emu/images
   ```

## Host System Requirements

### Basic Configuration
- FreeBSD 14.0 or later
- No special requirements

### Standard Configuration
- FreeBSD 14.0 or later
- MAC framework enabled in kernel
- Sufficient system resources (4GB+ RAM recommended)

### High Configuration
- FreeBSD 14.0 or later
- MAC framework enabled in kernel
- MAC veriexec module loaded
- At least 8GB RAM recommended
- Swap encryption requires memory encryption capable CPU (AES-NI)

### Maximum Configuration
- FreeBSD 14.0 or later
- MAC framework enabled in kernel
- MAC veriexec module loaded with fingerprints configured
- At least 16GB RAM recommended
- CPU affinity requires system with 4+ cores
- All memory encryption features require capable CPU

## Kernel Module Loading

Load the emulation framework kernel module:

```bash
# As root
kldload emu_core
```

To load at boot, add to `/etc/rc.conf`:

```
emu_load="YES"
```

## Verification

Verify the module is loaded:

```bash
kldstat | grep emu_core
```

Check sysctl settings:

```bash
sysctl kern.emulation
```

## Documentation

See the following man pages for more information:

- `emu(8)` - Emulation framework command reference
- `emu.conf(5)` - Configuration file format

## Troubleshooting

### Module fails to load
Check dmesg for errors:
```bash
dmesg | tail -50
```

### Permission denied errors
Ensure you have appropriate privileges or are running as root.

### Configuration not being read
Check that `/usr/local/etc/emu/emu.conf` exists and is readable.
